---
import TextPage from '../layouts/TextPage.astro';
import Contact from '../components/Contact.astro';
import { pageHref } from '../i18n';
---

<TextPage
  lang="en"
  page="support"
  title="Support"
  description="Answers to common questions about Collarbell: reminders on Android and iPhone, AI reading, the passport copy, deleting your account."
>
  <p slot="intro">
    Answers to common questions. If yours isn’t here, write to the developer: the contact is at the end of the
    page.
  </p>

  <div class="faq">
    <section class="card faq-item" aria-labelledby="android-reminders">
      <h2 id="android-reminders">Reminders don’t arrive on my Android phone</h2>
      <p>
        First, check that notifications are allowed for Collarbell in the phone’s settings. In the app, More →
        Notifications shows whether reminders reach this phone and has a “Send a test notification” button.
      </p>
      <p>
        On Xiaomi (HyperOS, MIUI) and some other phones, the system stops apps in the background to save battery.
        Allow Autostart for Collarbell and turn off battery restrictions for it (set battery saving to “No
        restrictions”). These settings are named a little differently on different phones.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="card faq-item" aria-labelledby="iphone">
      <h2 id="iphone">Are there reminders on iPhone?</h2>
      <p>Not yet: reminders on iPhone are coming later. Until then, everything due is on the Today screen.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="card faq-item" aria-labelledby="ai">
      <h2 id="ai">AI takes long to read a photo, or gets something wrong</h2>
      <p>
        Reading a photo takes up to a minute or two. AI can misread handwriting, dates or numbers, so check every
        field of the draft against the original before you save it. Nothing is saved until you do.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="card faq-item" aria-labelledby="passport">
      <h2 id="passport">Is the digital passport an official document?</h2>
      <p>
        No. It is a copy for your own use. The paper passport stays the official document, for example at the vet
        or when travelling.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="card faq-item" aria-labelledby="delete">
      <h2 id="delete">How do I delete my account?</h2>
      <p>
        See <a href={pageHref('en', 'deleteAccount')}>Delete your account</a>: what is deleted and how to ask for
        it.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="card faq-item" aria-labelledby="price">
      <h2 id="price">Is Collarbell free?</h2>
      <p>Yes, while it is in testing.</p>
    </section>
  </div>

  <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
  <Contact lang="en" subject="Collarbell support" />
</TextPage>
